---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LabNavigation from '../../components/LabNavigation.astro';
import OverviewHeader from '../../components/OverviewHeader.astro';
import ImageLab from '../../components/image-lab/ImageLab.astro';
import {siteConfig} from '../../site-config';
import {withBase} from 'astro-theme-university/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Image lab" description="Measure how JPEG compression changes image-based FID, with real Inception features extracted locally in your browser." mainAttrs={{class:'image-lab-main'}} {...siteConfig}>
  <div class="image-lab-page">
    <LabNavigation current="image-lab" />
    <OverviewHeader kicker="SLOP8412 / Image lab / Prototype 02">
      <Fragment slot="title">Same photograph.<br/>A different measurement.</Fragment>
      <p>Changing how images are encoded can change FID without changing what they depict. Put compressed pixels beside their originals, then measure what the feature extractor sees.</p>
    </OverviewHeader>
    <aside><strong>Actual image features. A deliberately tiny experiment.</strong> The supplied demo uses eight overlapping crops from one photograph, not eight independent dataset samples. You can also select 2–8 local images and transform their candidate copies. Neither experiment is a generative-model benchmark: these tiny sample estimates cannot establish model quality.</aside>
    <ImageLab />
    <section class="il-follow"><h2>Carry the observation back to the bench</h2>
      <p>The <a href={withBase('/sessions/04-getting-it-right/')}>Week 4 measurement contract</a> must specify preprocessing as well as the model. The <a href={withBase('/lectures/week-05/')}>Week 5 lecture</a> explains why a small empirical score is not the population quantity. Record which pixels changed, what stayed fixed, and what you cannot conclude in your <a href={withBase('/assessments/measurement-log/')}>measurement log</a>.</p>
      <p class="credit">Image: NASA / Eileen Collins, via <a href="https://scikit-image.org/docs/0.20.x/api/skimage.data.html#skimage.data.astronaut">scikit-image</a> (public domain). Deterministic crops and JPEG fixtures generated by this project. Encoder: <a href="https://github.com/mseitzer/pytorch-fid">pytorch-fid</a>, converted to ONNX; <a href={withBase('/image-lab/FID-LICENSE.txt')}>model redistribution licence</a>. No images are uploaded. Downloaded assets may remain in your browser cache; results last until you leave or refresh unless you export them.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  :global(.at-main.image-lab-main){grid-column:full;display:block;padding:0;}
  :global(body:has(.image-lab-main)::after){display:none;}
  .image-lab-page{max-width:1440px;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;margin:auto;padding:2.5rem clamp(1rem,4vw,4rem);}
  aside{border-left:2px solid var(--at-primary);padding:.5rem 1rem;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7;max-width:95ch;}
  .il-follow{max-width:85ch;line-height:1.75;margin-top:2rem;}.il-follow h2{color:var(--at-link);font-size:1.5rem;}.credit{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--at-text-muted);}
</style>
